<p>Republic of Congo President Denis Sassou Nguesso has won re-election with 94.82% of the vote, according to provisional results that Interior Minister Raymond Zephyrin Mboulou announced on national television. The result extends the 82-year-old leader&#x27;s rule in the Central African oil producer. The win gives Sassou Nguesso a fifth consecutive term and continues a rule that reports say has lasted nearly 42 years. Le Monde noted that the result still needs validation by the constitutional court.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/LBkJZ3em9Nj3KkTIC8EGgMYEi7y7TqaSfWnhgbUaVCEXYtQOyR-rBO-igOecaSBoVGVTbKQcyk22wV7vJ_yyv8ixmiDqiYq91j_Uv9ta7WfRLVtrupM4YTiOY-Sy-XEjJKgOcBL5Ec_PKP1kcnTPbZGI_EtKSSA1eH9bkA2Sp1p6zxlt1V2I_a2eg2sS3j05ifr3E7xvf8mk9-XX6HTjRiXnjcjp5i83Re_75ordA1OOdoOF5JRVhlk0M7fw4swFkQk-' alt='Incumbent President of the Republic of Congo, Denis Sassou Nguesso, who is running for re-election, speaks after casting his vote during the presidential election at a polling station in Brazzaville, Republic of Congo, March 15, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>The Straits Times called the election a tightly controlled vote. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/congo-republic-president-sassou-nguesso-wins-re-election-state-tv-reports'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>Le Monde reported that the result is still provisional until the constitutional court validates it. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/03/17/congo-brazzaville-s-sassou-nguesso-is-reelected-according-to-provisional-results_6751541_4.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/congo-republic-president-sassou-nguesso-wins-re-election-state-tv-reports'>Congo Republic&#x27;s Sassou wins re-election with nearly 95% in tightly controlled vote</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/03/17/congo-brazzaville-s-sassou-nguesso-is-reelected-according-to-provisional-resu